     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi D-RUGgies,<div><br></div><div>Hope all is well. I apologize for the delayed email this week. Brandon gave a great talk with a very good overview of list-columns, operating on lists with the family of functions <font face=\"monospace, monospace\"><b>map</b></font> and <font face=\"monospace, monospace\" style=\"font-weight:bold\">walk </font><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">from the <b><a href=\"http://purrr.tidyverse.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://purrr.tidyverse.org/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466693467000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1HTLdqTQPb-IGJr1WoKCRU\">purrr</a></b> package. We attempted to record/youtube-cast the talk, but somehow the recording has been lost in the ether (i.e., I think I set it up wrong and now it&#39;s vanished). I think I have it sorted out for future talks, so we&#39;ll get some recordings up soon. My apologies...</font></div><div><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Good news! All his material is online! See the great slides, Rmd Notebook, etc. on the D-RUG website here:</font></div><div><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><ul><li><b><a href=\"http://d-rug.github.io/blog/2017/Brandon-Hurr-on-using-map-and-walk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://d-rug.github.io/blog/2017/Brandon-Hurr-on-using-map-and-walk&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466693467000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3cpegyI3QFVTZmzofPSYNI\">http://d-rug.github.io/blog/2017/Brandon-Hurr-on-using-map-and-walk</a><br></b></li></ul></div><div><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><b><u>Package/Functions of the Week:</u></b></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\">This week I think the two packages that make sense to highlight are the purrr package (see Brandon&#39;s talk for details, examples, etc) and the<span style=\"font-size:small;font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"> </span><b style=\"font-size:small;font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-style:italic\"><a href=\"https://slides.yihui.name/xaringan/#1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://slides.yihui.name/xaringan/%231&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466693467000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hcG8PERnuRLtGSxVJdPNa\">xaringan</a> </b><span style=\"font-size:small;font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">package<b><i>. </i></b></span></div></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><span style=\"font-size:small;font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><b><i><br></i></b></span></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><span style=\"font-size:small;font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><b>xaringan</b> is a very cool little package that allows you to create html slide presentations in RStudio. I just recently used it to give a talk at a conference, and I was pretty happy with the result (see slides <a href=\"https://ryanpeek.github.io/slides/20171025/2017_CA_SFS.html#1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://ryanpeek.github.io/slides/20171025/2017_CA_SFS.html%231&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466693468000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0436dU_ojv99G1alwCflOH\">here</a>). As long as you have internet connectivity, you can build in interactive slides, link to web content, and customize away. In addition you can print to pdf from your browser as a nice backup. </span></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><span style=\"font-size:small;font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><br></span></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><span style=\"font-size:small;font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">Take a look!</span></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><span style=\"font-size:small;font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\"><br></span></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><span style=\"font-size:small;font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">Adios,</span></div><div style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><span style=\"font-size:small;font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">Ryan</span></div><div><div><br></div>-- <br><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br><span style=\"line-height:19px\"><font face=\"times new roman, serif\"><i><b><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;float:none;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);display:inline\"><span> </span></span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"></b></i></font></span><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><font size=\"1\"><i>&quot;When we try to pick out anything by itself